1
00:00:00,119 --> 00:00:02,039
Jesus told his hometown one old story

2
00:00:02,519 --> 00:00:03,240
— and they tried to throw him

3
00:00:03,279 --> 00:00:03,819
off a cliff.

4
00:00:04,619 --> 00:00:05,739
This is the story.

5
00:00:07,039 --> 00:00:07,359
Naaman:

6
00:00:07,679 --> 00:00:09,119
a great general — and a leper.

7
00:00:09,699 --> 00:00:10,859
A servant girl pointed him to a

8
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:11,300
prophet.

9
00:00:11,679 --> 00:00:12,879
Elisha didn't even come out.

10
00:00:13,159 --> 00:00:13,979
He sent one line:

11
00:00:14,579 --> 00:00:16,260
wash in the Jordan, seven times.

12
00:00:17,079 --> 00:00:18,039
Naaman was furious:

13
00:00:18,899 --> 00:00:21,639
"Are not Abana and Pharpar, rivers of

14
00:00:21,719 --> 00:00:24,359
Damascus, better than all the waters of

15
00:00:24,459 --> 00:00:24,879
Israel?

16
00:00:25,399 --> 00:00:26,979
may I not wash in them, and

17
00:00:27,039 --> 00:00:28,979
be clean?" His own servants stopped him:

18
00:00:30,579 --> 00:00:32,700
"My father, if the prophet had bid

19
00:00:32,739 --> 00:00:34,860
thee do some great thing, wouldest thou

20
00:00:34,899 --> 00:00:35,539
not have done it?

21
00:00:36,279 --> 00:00:38,059
how much rather then, when he saith

22
00:00:38,099 --> 00:00:40,399
to thee, Wash, and be clean?" He

23
00:00:40,459 --> 00:00:41,039
went down.

24
00:00:41,739 --> 00:00:43,199
He washed, seven times.

25
00:00:43,879 --> 00:00:45,319
New skin, like a child's.

26
00:00:46,579 --> 00:00:48,040
This is the story Jesus told —

27
00:00:48,099 --> 00:00:49,840
centuries later, to his own hometown:

28
00:00:51,239 --> 00:00:52,939
"Many lepers were in Israel in the

29
00:00:52,959 --> 00:00:54,939
time of Eliseus the prophet;

30
00:00:54,979 --> 00:00:57,180
and none of them was cleansed, saving

31
00:00:57,279 --> 00:01:01,000
Naaman the Syrian." The best thing Naaman

32
00:01:01,039 --> 00:01:02,180
ever did was lose an argument.

33
00:01:02,959 --> 00:01:04,300
If the cure feels beneath you —

34
00:01:04,339 --> 00:01:06,520
too plain, too easy, too small —

35
00:01:06,559 --> 00:01:07,479
that's the same argument.

36
00:01:08,180 --> 00:01:08,959
It's still worth losing.
